            "description": "This dataset compiles country-level information on national hydrogen strategies. It includes UN Geoscheme macro-regions, ISO 3166 country codes, national hydrogen strategy status, hydrogen trade status, potential trade, domestic demand, expected production, expected electrolyser capacity, hydrogen-colour references, infrastructure references, reasons for national hydrogen strategies, bilateral agreements or MoUs, and row-level references. The table contains 196 country or territory rows and 29 columns after removal of the original remarks column. Quantitative target values are stored as text to preserve ranges, inequalities, and source-specific notes. ECOWAS member-state rows may include information from the collective ECOWAS hydrogen strategy; these values represent collective targets rather than individual national targets. Non-English strategy documents were translated for data collection where required. Quantitative values were converted to TWh where necessary using the lower heating value of hydrogen of 33.3 kWh/kg. For electrolyser-capacity-based conversions, reported GW values were converted where required using assumed full load hours of 4000 h/y and efficiency of 65%. Low-carbon hydrogen was interpreted as including blue and green hydrogen unless stated otherwise. Infrastructure references and reasons for national hydrogen strategies were clustered into keyword lists. The bilateral-agreement field lists only countries explicitly stated in the national hydrogen strategies.",
